.TH KEA 1 "" "kea" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kea \- a second brain that checks its facts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.RS 4
.nf
kea [\-\-brain PATH] <command> [options] [\-\-json]
kea init [PATH] [\-\-example]
kea status | check | state | roadmap
kea log TEXT | fact NAME VALUE | decide TITLE | predict CLAIM | score ID OUTCOME
kea search QUERY | show ID | ingest [SOURCE [PATH]] | effort
kea plan new SLUG | brief SLUG | council SLUG | synth SLUG | seats
kea mcp | skill install | digest [TRANSCRIPT] | guide | man
.fi
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
kea keeps a second brain for you and your AI agents in a folder of plain Markdown. It holds facts with their sources and dates, decisions with the date to look at them again, predictions with a confidence that get scored when their date comes, a roadmap of open work, and plans that a council of independent AI models reviews before you commit to them. Next to the folder, kea keeps a local search index over your past AI agent sessions (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode), your ChatGPT and Claude exports, your git history and your notes, every hit traceable to its exact source.
.PP
It is built around one idea: a fact without a source and a date is an assumption, and an AI agent that cannot tell the two apart will repeat your guesses back to you as truth. kea makes the difference visible, lints it, and scores your predictions against what happened, so the brain gets better with use instead of only bigger.
.PP
kea is one Python package with no dependencies beyond the standard library. It runs on Python 3.15. Nothing leaves your machine except a council packet you choose to send.
.SH QUICK START
.RS 4
.nf
uv tool install git+https://github.com/jpsanders/kea   # uv fetches Python 3.15 when you lack it
kea init ~/brain                                        # make a brain; it becomes your default
cd ~/brain && kea status                                # the whole brain at a glance
kea skill install                                       # teach Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode to use it
kea ingest claude\-code                                  # make your past agent sessions searchable
kea search "what did we decide about pricing"
.fi
.RE
.PP
To explore first, make the example brain, a made up coffee roastery with facts, decisions, scored predictions and a plan the council reviewed: \fBkea init /tmp/tidewater \-\-example\fR.
.SH THE BRAIN
.PP
A brain is a folder with a \fBkea.toml\fR in it. \fBkea init\fR lays these files down; every one is plain Markdown that people and agents edit by hand next to the CLI.
.TP
ROADMAP.md
Open work: waiting for the owner, next, running by itself, dates. Start every session here
.TP
STATE.md
What is true now: a facts table (fact, value, source, verified) and a dated log, newest first
.TP
DECISIONS.md
Decisions D-0001 onwards: the decision, why, status, and when to revisit
.TP
PREDICTIONS.md
Predictions P-0001 onwards: a claim, a date, a confidence, and the outcome once scored
.TP
IDEAS.md
Parked ideas I-0001 onwards, in the words they arrived in. Nothing here is active
.TP
METRICS.md
Measured numbers only; NOT MEASURED rows keep the measurement debt visible
.TP
LEARNING.md
What reality taught the brain, and which council seats were right
.TP
SOURCES.md
What to import and why; canonical sources that win any argument
.TP
VOICE.md
How agents should write for the owner
.TP
AGENTS.md
How any AI agent works in this brain; CLAUDE.md imports it
.TP
frameworks/
Lenses for thinking, each with boundary conditions and a retrodiction score
.TP
plans/
One folder per plan: proposal, questions, reviews, synthesis, production plan, execution log
.TP
council/
PROTOCOL.md, the rules, and roster.toml, the seats
.TP
journal/
Execution logs and the notes a STATE.md entry points to
.TP
\&.kea/
The local search index. Never committed; delete it any time and kea ingest rebuilds it
.PP
Entries are headings kea can read back: \fB### D\-0002 · 2026\-11\-13 · Title\fR followed by \fB\- **Field:** value\fR lines. Keep that shape when you edit by hand and every other line you write is left exactly as it is.
.SH THE RULES
.PP
These rules are the point of the system. The CLI, the skills and the MCP server all enforce or teach them.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBVerified facts only.\fR A fact lives in STATE.md with a source and a date. Anything else is UNVERIFIED and says how
.PP
it would be checked.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNever present an estimate as a measurement.\fR Measured numbers go in METRICS.md with their source.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLog decisions\fR with the reasoning and a revisit date or trigger. Unlogged reasoning does not compound.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWrite predictions down and score them.\fR A prediction names a number and a date, and anyone could score it.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBImport distilled, not raw.\fR Raw exports stay where they are; name the decision a source changes before you
.PP
import it.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFrameworks only with boundary conditions.\fR A lens cited outside the stage it fits manufactures false confidence.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBConsensus is a signal, not a verdict.\fR Models share training data and blind spots; every synthesis says what
.PP
every seat missed.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAsk, do not assume.\fR Questions only the owner can answer go on the roadmap under waiting.
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
Every command that prints data takes \fB\-\-json\fR and prints one JSON document with stable fields. \fB\-\-brain PATH\fR before the command picks the brain. Dates accept \fB2026\-12\-01\fR, \fBtoday\fR, \fBtomorrow\fR, or an offset such as \fB+30d\fR, \fB+6w\fR or \fB+3m\fR.
.SS Start and look
.TP
kea init [PATH]
Make a brain; --name, --owner, --example, --force, --no-git, --default, --no-default
.TP
kea status
The whole brain: freshness, due decisions and predictions, roadmap, plans, seats, evidence, health
.TP
kea check
Lint: unsourced facts, facts past recheck, malformed entries, overdue items. Exit 1 on errors; --strict
.TP
kea state
The facts and the newest log entries; --entries N
.TP
kea roadmap
Open items, numbered, and the dates
.SS Write to the ledger
.TP
kea log TEXT
A dated entry at the top of STATE.md's log; --title, --source
.TP
kea fact NAME VALUE --source S
Record or update a fact; --verified DATE (default today)
.TP
kea decide TITLE --decision D
Log a decision; --why, --revisit DATE or trigger, --source
.TP
kea decisions
Active decisions; --due for those past their revisit date, --all for closed ones too
.TP
kea revisit ID --outcome O
Close the loop: --status, --surprise 0 to 10, --lesson, --next DATE
.TP
kea predict CLAIM --by DATE --confidence N
A prediction from 0 to 100; --plan SLUG, --decision D-0003
.TP
kea score ID OUTCOME
Score it: true, false, partial (counts half) or void (left out); --note
.TP
kea predictions
Every prediction; --due, --open
.TP
kea calibration
Brier score, skill over a coin, and calibration buckets
.TP
kea idea TEXT
Park an idea; --why. kea ideas lists them
.TP
kea roadmap add TEXT
Add to next; --waiting for the owner, --running for jobs
.TP
kea roadmap done N
Close item N (or a unique piece of its text); --proof
.SS Search the evidence
.TP
kea ingest SOURCE [PATH]
Index a source locally. Sources: claude-code, codex, opencode, chatgpt, claude, git, docs
.TP
kea ingest
Scan the brain and every source ingested before again; unchanged files are skipped
.TP
kea search QUERY
Best matches first; --kind, --platform, --mine, --since DATE, --limit N, --any
.TP
kea show ID
One hit in full with its source; --context N shows the turns around it
.TP
kea sources
What the index was read from, with errors
.TP
kea forget ID
Delete a source and everything read from it; --kind KIND for every source of one kind
.TP
kea effort
Your own prompts to AI agents per project: where attention went; --months, --since
.TP
kea digest [TRANSCRIPT]
A Claude Code session as digest.md, prompts.md, turns.md and meta.json; -o DIR, --tz
.SS Plans and the council
.TP
kea plan new SLUG
Start a plan from the template
.TP
kea plan
Every plan, its stage, and its next step
.TP
kea brief SLUG
Build the packet every seat reads, hashed; --show prints it
.TP
kea council SLUG
Send the packet to every ready seat in parallel; --seat, --resume, --dry-run, --yes
.TP
kea synth SLUG
The synthesis scaffold: verdicts, convergence, splits, solo insights
.TP
kea seats
The seats and whether each can run; --probe asks each to answer
.SS Agents and docs
.TP
kea mcp
Serve the brain to agents over the Model Context Protocol on stdio
.TP
kea skill install
Copy kea's skills into every agent found; --agent claude, codex, opencode or agents; --dry-run
.TP
kea skill show [NAME]
Print a skill, for agents without a skills folder
.TP
kea guide
Print this manual as Markdown
.TP
kea man
Show the man page; --install so plain man kea works, --raw for the roff
.SH FINDING THE BRAIN
.PP
kea looks, in order: \fB\-\-brain PATH\fR, then \fB$KEA_BRAIN\fR, then the current folder and each parent, then the default brain named in \fB~/.config/kea/config.toml\fR. The first \fBkea init\fR sets the default. A folder without \fBkea.toml\fR is never treated as a brain, so notes kea did not make are never touched.
.SH EVIDENCE
.PP
\fBkea ingest\fR reads, never writes, and redacts before it stores. Each source and where kea looks by default:
.TP
claude-code
\fB$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects\fR or ~/.claude/projects: your prompts and the replies; no tool calls
.TP
codex
\fB$CODEX_HOME/sessions\fR or ~/.codex/sessions: prompts and replies; injected context is skipped
.TP
opencode
~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db, opened read only: the text of every session
.TP
chatgpt
Your data export: the zip, its folder, or conversations.json; the kept branch of each chat
.TP
claude
Your Claude.ai export: conversations, and the documents in projects
.TP
git
A repository or a folder of them: every commit on every branch, with its files
.TP
docs
A folder of .md, .txt, .rst and .org files, split into sections by heading
.PP
The brain's own Markdown is indexed too, and refreshed before every search. Your commits and your prompts are marked as yours, so \fBkea search \-\-mine\fR and \fBkea effort\fR work: set \fB[identity]\fR in kea.toml, or kea reads your global git config. A second run reads only what changed. Every hit carries a ref: a file and line, an export member and message id, or a repository and commit.
.SH THE COUNCIL
.PP
Independent models review a plan from one byte identical packet. No seat sees another seat's review. The Chair is the agent you work with: it reviews first, from the packet alone, and writes the synthesis last.
.RS 4
.nf
kea plan new 2026\-12\-pricing     # write 00\-proposal.md and 01\-review\-questions.md
kea brief 2026\-12\-pricing        # build and hash the packet
                                 # the Chair reviews from the packet alone
kea council 2026\-12\-pricing      # every ready seat, in parallel
kea synth 2026\-12\-pricing        # the scaffold; the Chair writes 11\-synthesis.md
kea decide ... && kea predict ... \-\-plan 2026\-12\-pricing
.fi
.RE
.PP
Seats live in \fBcouncil/roster.toml\fR. Each names a provider and a model; lineage matters more than raw strength, so the default roster mixes Google, DeepSeek, OpenAI open weights, Mistral and two local models. A seat whose key variable is not set, or whose local server is not running, is skipped.
.TP
gemini
GEMINI_API_KEY
.TP
anthropic
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
.TP
openai
OPENAI_API_KEY
.TP
mistral
MISTRAL_API_KEY
.TP
groq
GROQ_API_KEY
.TP
cerebras
CEREBRAS_API_KEY
.TP
nvidia
NVIDIA_API_KEY
.TP
openrouter
OPENROUTER_API_KEY
.TP
deepseek
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
.TP
xai
XAI_API_KEY
.TP
ollama, lmstudio
none: they run on this machine
.PP
Any other OpenAI compatible server works with \fBbase_url\fR and \fBkey_env\fR. Calls to one provider are spaced by the roster's \fB[rate_limits]\fR. Keys travel only in headers, never in a URL, and never over plain HTTP to another machine.
.PP
The packet holds the files in \fB[brief] include\fR and the plan. Free tiers may keep or train on what they receive, so \fBkea council\fR asks before it sends anything off the machine; \fB\-\-yes\fR skips the question and \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR shows what would go where.
.SH CALIBRATION
.PP
\fBkea calibration\fR scores every prediction marked true, false or partial. The Brier score is the mean of the squared gap between the confidence you stated and what happened: 0 is perfect, 0.25 is what always saying 50% earns. Skill is how much better than that coin you are. The buckets show, for each band of stated confidence, how often those predictions came true: if your 80% predictions come true half the time, you are overconfident there.
.SH AGENTS
.PP
kea is made to be used by AI agents as much as by people.
.PP
\fBSkills.\fR \fBkea skill install\fR copies three skills into every agent folder it finds: ~/.claude/skills, ~/.codex/skills, ~/.config/opencode/skills and ~/.agents/skills. kea teaches the rules and the session routine, kea-council runs a council review, kea-frameworks turns a source into a framework.
.PP
\fBClaude Code plugin.\fR The repository is a plugin with the skills and the MCP server:
.RS 4
.nf
/plugin marketplace add jpsanders/kea
/plugin install kea@kea
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBMCP server.\fR \fBkea mcp\fR speaks the Model Context Protocol on stdio. Tools: brain_status, state, search, show, decisions, predictions, roadmap, check, plans, seats, effort, log_entry, record_fact, decide, revisit_decision, predict, score_prediction, add_idea, roadmap_add, roadmap_done, plan_new, brief, synth, ingest and council_run. Read tools are marked read only; council_run sends data off the machine and needs confirm set to true. Resources expose STATE.md, ROADMAP.md, DECISIONS.md, PREDICTIONS.md and AGENTS.md; prompts start_session, end_session and chair_review appear as slash commands in clients that show them.
.PP
Claude Code, for every project:
.RS 4
.nf
claude mcp add \-\-scope user kea \-\- kea mcp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Codex, in ~/.codex/config.toml:
.RS 4
.nf
[mcp_servers.kea]
command = "kea"
args = ["mcp"]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Cursor (~/.cursor/mcp.json), Gemini CLI (~/.gemini/settings.json) and Claude Desktop take the same JSON:
.RS 4
.nf
{"mcpServers": {"kea": {"command": "kea", "args": ["mcp"], "env": {"KEA_BRAIN": "/home/you/brain"}}}}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Without kea installed, use \fBuvx\fR as the command and \fB\-\-from git+https://github.com/jpsanders/kea kea mcp\fR as the arguments; the first start downloads it. Set \fBKEA_BRAIN\fR where the client starts servers outside your projects.
.SH FILES
.TP
kea.toml
Marks a brain; settings for the brain, the packet, your identity and ingest
.TP
\&.kea/index.sqlite
The local search index, one per brain
.TP
council/briefing/
Built packets; ignored by git
.TP
~/.config/kea/config.toml
Your default brain
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
KEA_BRAIN
The brain to use when --brain is not given
.TP
KEA_TODAY, KEA_NOW
Fix the date or the time, for reproducible demos and tests
.TP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME
Where the config and the man page go
.TP
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME
Where Claude Code and Codex keep sessions and skills
.TP
NO_COLOR
Plain output, no colour
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0 on success. 1 when a command fails, when kea check finds an error (or a warning, with --strict), or when no seat returned. 2 for a mistake in the arguments. With --json, a failure also prints {"error": "..."}.
.SH PRIVACY AND SECURITY
.PP
Everything stays on your machine: the brain is your folder, and the index is a SQLite file inside it that git ignores. kea never reads paths that name a credential store (.ssh, .aws, .env, .gnupg, credentials, secrets and more; add your own under [ingest] deny), and it replaces anything shaped like a key or token with [REDACTED] before storing text. The only network calls are the council seats you configure and run. Report security problems privately: https://github.com/jpsanders/kea/security/advisories/new
.SH PERFORMANCE
.PP
kea starts in milliseconds: Python 3.15's lazy imports load only what a command uses. The index is SQLite with FTS5 and BM25 ranking; ingest runs in one transaction per source and skips anything unchanged. Measured on one Linux machine, 1.3 GB of Claude Code transcripts index in about five seconds, a second run takes a tenth of a second, and a search answers in about 50 ms.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
kea fact "Cash on hand" "EUR 18,400" \-\-source "bank export" \-\-verified 2026\-11\-10
kea decide "Test wholesale first" \-\-decision "Five sample bags before any lease" \-\-revisit +30d
kea predict "Three of five cafes order" \-\-by +14d \-\-confidence 60 \-\-plan second\-cafe
kea score P\-0007 partial \-\-note "two ordered, see journal/wholesale.md"
kea search "flat white price" \-\-since 2026\-01\-01 \-\-json
kea ingest git ~/code && kea search "migration" \-\-mine \-\-kind commit
kea council second\-cafe \-\-dry\-run
kea roadmap add "Decide on the Harbour Street lease" \-\-waiting
.fi
.RE
